answer/id #uuid "335d00d7-a3e1-54c1-806f-71e188bfe45c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$3.36$ per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27dc373a-341a-5b2e-be8c-b865424cfaa0" :answer/id #uuid "27dc373a-341a-5b2e-be8c-b865424cfaa0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$3.50$ per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfffb0d4-abcf-56fb-a029-c104e068368d" :answer/id #uuid "bfffb0d4-abcf-56fb-a029-c104e068368d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$4.02$ per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ae98ebc-c4ae-5b45-ad32-87ba2b191e0d" :answer/id #uuid "2ae98ebc-c4ae-5b45-ad32-87ba2b191e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$4.10$ per gallon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7148b05-c37b-56db-9e21-9c51d5a86ad3" :question/id #uuid "b7148b05-c37b-56db-9e21-9c51d5a86ad3" :question/math-academy-id "q-68547" :question/problem "A pack contains $24$ fluid ounce of cream cheese and costs $$6.00.$ What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$  \n\n$$\n24÷8=3\n$$\n\nSo, $24$ fluid ounces is the same as $3$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $3:$ \n\n$$\n6.00÷3=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cream cheese costs $$2.00$ per cup." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c14baa77-de49-5b0a-b3aa-d1c3e71903fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c14baa77-de49-5b0a-b3aa-d1c3e71903fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "c14baa77-de49-5b0a-b3aa-d1c3e71903fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3fdc82a0-9a27-58fb-b6e8-c19566c4f986" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1efe9830-e903-5ad3-a8c7-c7731a61db0c" "answer-d0f3ba0d-c418-5d69-88a6-