 the line rises vertically per unit that it runs horizontally.\n\nSince the graph decreases ($↘$) as we go from left to right, the line rises by a negative amount.\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-845d3982-0f38-5a31-810f-b6e038ecbee7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-845d3982-0f38-5a31-810f-b6e038ecbee7" :answer-field/id #uuid "845d3982-0f38-5a31-810f-b6e038ecbee7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e42a8251-dec1-5e57-810b-6a64baa82cce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e42a8251-dec1-5e57-810b-6a64baa82cce" "answer-a3055d8e-02f8-5c6b-9d08-3e0f1c8c247c" "answer-882f8417-b97a-55e7-b84a-177f0eeb323f" "answer-e7e48cab-a94e-569b-b463-524076435452" "answer-3d057346-e893-5b56-91c9-02634ef0bcb7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e42a8251-dec1-5e57-810b-6a64baa82cce" :answer/id #uuid "e42a8251-dec1-5e57-810b-6a64baa82cce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Negative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3055d8e-02f8-5c6b-9d08-3e0f1c8c247c" :answer/id #uuid "a3055d8e-02f8-5c6b-9d08-3e0f1c8c247c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Not enough information" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-882f8417-b97a-55e7-b84a-177f0eeb323f" :answer/id #uuid "882f8417-b97a-55e7-b84a-177f0eeb323f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Positive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7e48cab-a94e-569b-b463-524076435452" :answer/id #uuid "e7e48cab-a94e-569b-b463-524076435452" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d057346-e893-5b56-91c9-02634ef0bcb7" :answer/id #uuid "3d057346-e893-5b56-91c9-02634ef0bcb7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Zero" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068893 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e554ee9f-50e5-5692-8b77-359b451c2bbf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e554ee9f-50e5-5692-8b77-359b451c2bbf" :question/id #uuid "e554ee9f-50e5-5692-8b77-359b451c2bbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-26721" :question/problem "![](images/20/2026a71a7cb647e7a5d844e9c5259f73321d7fd8097255245dc99f87dfc60a92.png)\n\nThe straight line shown above intersects the $y$-axis when $y=5$ and intersects the $x$-axis when $x=7.$ Find its slope." :question/worked-solution "Note that the line passes through the points $(0,5)$ and $(7,0).$ So, we let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,0),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-5}{7-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $-\\frac{5}{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c796a5cc-7470-555e-8c4a-e7fb39dc2c3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c796a5cc-7470-555e-8c4a-e7fb39dc2c3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c796a5cc-7470-555e-8c4a-e7fb39dc2c3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b734c1fc-7b80-5cc1-bb58-37307d83cd9e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b78ba8a4-7052-5d26-92c7-8724b2179bd5" "answer-e729bea2-1620-507c-a9ae-744cc39dcf39" "answer-b734c1fc-7b80-5cc1-bb58-37307d83cd9e" "answer-6c973c76-cd0c-5576-8885-0c465bab546c" "answer-4b675aa5-7ca8-5a20-8b98-50a672fad62c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b78ba8a4-7052-5d26-92c7-8724b2179bd5" :answer/id #uuid "b78ba8a4-7052-5d26-92c7-8724b2179bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e729bea2-1620-507c-a9ae-744cc39dcf39" :answer/id #uuid "e729bea2-1620-507c-a9ae-744cc39dcf39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b734c1fc-7b80-5cc1-bb58-37307d83cd9e" :answer/id #uuid "b734c1fc-7b80-5cc1-bb58-37307d83cd9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c973c76-cd0c-5576-8885-0c465bab546c" :answer/id #uuid "6c973c76-cd0c-5576-8885-0c465bab546c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b675aa5-7ca8-5a20-8b98-50a672fad62c" :answer/id #uuid "4b675aa5-7ca8-5a20-8b98-50a672fad62c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068781 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d9d1c0c3-5c99-595f-9217-43cdc322907f" "question-4e8669dc-08f6-5619-b2c9-0ec5b114ec63"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9d1c0c3-5c99-595f-9217-43cdc322907f" :question/id #uuid "d9d1c0c3-5c99-595f-9217-43cdc322907f" :question/math-academy-id "q-44161" :question/problem "![](images/27/27763c2083cbfc9961a619fb8e4f9bbb50791f446b734aef2a4f822e5d04de4b.png)\n\nDetermine the slope of the line shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line is horizontal, and therefore it has a slope of zero.\n\n We can see this by choosing two points on the line, such as $(0,0)$ and $(3,0),$ and computing the slope between them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}=\\frac{0-0}{3-0}=\\frac{0}{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-902aa591-7b1f-510e-89d2-c56557cdce5e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-902aa591-7b1f-510e-89d2-c56557cdce5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "902aa591-7b1f-510e-89d2-c56557cdce5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-244abeff-5947-5d09-8904-4308c44b291c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5346ccb5-d421-5f50-8754-3b145bc626f9" "answer-244abeff-5947-5d09-8904-4308c44b291c" "answer-76f8dcbe-84e6-5ccc-bdd0-e597e93e0cce" "answer-86018d1a-f75a-561d-a449-f1a883