B$ and  $C$ have the lowest unit price of $$0.18/\\text{oz}.$ Therefore, boxes $B$ and $C$ offer the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce911441-7f5d-51d8-b75e-0b18a93a4e51"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce911441-7f5d-51d8-b75e-0b18a93a4e51" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce911441-7f5d-51d8-b75e-0b18a93a4e51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b64c3b4a-bb29-586f-840a-70997b94eb6a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2079d726-3520-5cc5-94e2-91ca16684711" "answer-78f24c6f-e216-5acb-8e29-463bf8a38116" "answer-a8e88bdd-cc49-58ec-9a7f-0ad19c2452ad" "answer-b64c3b4a-bb29-586f-840a-70997b94eb6a" "answer-be7604bc-90ba-593e-9e81-d9613f48d7e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2079d726-3520-5cc5-94e2-91ca16684711" :answer/id #uuid "2079d726-3520-5cc5-94e2-91ca16684711" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78f24c6f-e216-5acb-8e29-463bf8a38116" :answer/id #uuid "78f24c6f-e216-5acb-8e29-463bf8a38116" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8e88bdd-cc49-58ec-9a7f-0ad19c2452ad" :answer/id #uuid "a8e88bdd-cc49-58ec-9a7f-0ad19c2452ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b64c3b4a-bb29-586f-840a-70997b94eb6a" :answer/id #uuid "b64c3b4a-bb29-586f-840a-70997b94eb6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be7604bc-90ba-593e-9e81-d9613f48d7e8" :answer/id #uuid "be7604bc-90ba-593e-9e81-d9613f48d7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d34abd56-cdca-5fad-b44a-9d3b63e57048" :question/id #uuid "d34abd56-cdca-5fad-b44a-9d3b63e57048" :question/math-academy-id "q-355006" :question/problem "Sarah wonders what bag of coffee to buy from three different types available at the cafe:\n\n- Bag $A$ weighs $12$ ounces, and costs $$9.60\\,.$\n\n- Bag $B$ weighs $16$ ounces, and costs $$12.00\\,.$\n\n- Bag $C$ weighs $8$ ounces, and costs $$6.80\\,.$\n\nWhich bag of coffee is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of ounces.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in bag $A$, we get\n\n$$\n9.60÷12=0.80\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $$0.80$ per ounce.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in bag $B$, we get\n\n$$\n12.00÷16=0.75\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$0.75$ per ounce.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in bag $C$, we get\n\n$$\n6.80÷8=0.85\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $$0.85$ per ounce.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $B$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $B$ is the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd2d7248-3f1b-5a0e-8555-6ff860c97edc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd2d7248-3f1b-5a0e-8555-6ff860c97edc" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2d7248-3f1b-5a0e-8555-6ff860c97edc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-779ab6ef-6780-5dd8-828e-b29df0c5b4dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9b94a2e-51bb-5b5f-a4f8-1cdcc321acc2" "answer-40e3f585-edf1-517f-92ac-7bfe4b4a50fa" "answer-5d184d42-ba72-557f-8fb2-70492790ba10" "answer-779ab6ef-6780-5dd8-828e-b29df0c5b4dc" "answer-bd41aa29-8b8e-58da-98d7-399488cd0fe5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9b94a2e-51bb-5b5f-a4f8-1cdcc321acc2" :answer/id #uuid "c9b94a2e-51bb-5b5f-a4f8-1cdcc321acc2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40e3f585-edf1-517f-92ac-7bfe4b4a50fa" :answer/id #uuid "40e3f585-edf1-517f-92ac-7bfe4b4a50fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d184d42-ba72-557f-8fb2-70492790ba10" :answer/id #uuid "5d184d42-ba72-557f-8fb2-70492790ba10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-779ab6ef-6780-5dd8-828e-b29df0c5b4dc" :answer/id #uuid "779ab6ef-6780-5dd8-828e-b29df0c5b4dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd41aa29-8b8e-58da-98d7-399488cd0fe5" :answer/id #uuid "bd41aa29-8b8e-58da-98d7-399488cd0fe5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-60c429d6-78bf-52f4-a402-0b1e67fa2508" :question/id #uuid "60c429d6-78bf-52f4-a402-0b1e67fa2508" :question/math-academy-id "q-355005" :question/problem "David needs to decide what bag of flour to buy from three different types available at the grocery store:\n\n- Bag $A$ weighs $5$ kilograms, and costs $$7.50\\,.$\n\n- Bag $B$ weighs $2$ kilograms, and costs $$3.20\\,.$\n\n- Bag $C$ weighs $1$ kilogram, and costs $$1.70\\,.$\n\nWhich bag of flour is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of kilograms.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $A$, we get\n\n$$\n7.50÷5=1.50\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $$1.50$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $B$, we get\n\n$$\n3.20÷2=1.60\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$1.60$ per kilogram.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of kilograms in bag $C$, we get\n\n$$\n1.70÷1=1.70\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $$1.70$ per kilogram.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $A$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $A$ is the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1856c59-881f-5703-8688-905238b1066e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1856c59-881f-5703-8688-905238b1066e" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1856c59-881f-5703-8688-905238b1066e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-92f59a17-f5a0-5c24-bdb3-c57c8f1f241f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a67c690a-a1dc-5445-9741-577c1604442a" "answer-92f59a17-f5a0-5c24-bdb3-c57c8f1f241f" "answer-ad7ad806-1c43-582c-b01a-34db879f747e" "answer-e28759b2-e789-5d7c-847c-325d3f81b586" "answer-3044ea68-e73b-56dd-9a11-c82e1d203a05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a67c690a-a1dc-5445-9741-577c1604442a" :answer/id #uuid "a67c690a-a1dc-5445-9741-577c1604442a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92f59a17-f5a0-5c24-bdb3-c57c8f1f241f" :answer/id #uuid "92f59a17-f5a0-5c24-bdb3-c57c8f1f241f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad7ad806-1c43-582c-b01a-34db879f747e" :answer/id #uuid "ad7ad806-1c43-582c-b01a-34db879f747e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e28759b2-e789-5d7c-847c-325d3f81b586" :answer/id #uuid "e28759b2-e789-5d7c-847c-325d3f81b586" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3044ea68-e73b-56dd-9a11-c82e1d203a05" :answer/id #uuid "3044ea68-e73b-56dd-9a11-c82e1d203a05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1900fcae-3d76-5147-a463-152f960f7a6c" :question/id #uuid "1900fcae-3d76-5147-a463-152f960f7a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-68909" :question/problem "Martha wonders what bag of oranges to buy from three different types available at the supermarket:\n\n- Bag $A$ weighs $10$ pounds, and costs $$13.30\\,.$\n\n- Bag $B$ weighs $8$ pounds, and costs $$11.20\\,.$\n\n- Bag $C$ weighs $6$ pounds, and costs $$9.00\\,.$\n\nWhich bag of oranges is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of pounds.  \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in bag $A$,  we get\n\n$$\n13.30÷10=1.33\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $$1.33$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in bag $B$,  we get\n\n$$\n11.20÷8=1.40\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$1.40$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in bag $C$,  we get\n\n$$\n9.00÷6=1.50\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $$1.50$  per pound.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $A$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $A$ is the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-291a271a-4e84-53aa-a84e-1fa55fac9dd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-291a271a-4e84-53aa-a84e-1fa55fac9dd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "291a271a-4e84-53aa-a84e-1fa55fac9dd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4be9c323-4eec-53ad-ae4b-9e07303bdcb4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1906510-55d6-5ff1-aac1-ff539fe0295c" "answer-4be9c323-4eec-53ad-ae4b-9e07303bdcb4" "answer-9e1fc3e9-6b7e-5bb9-b995-f286738d3db4" "answer-43e0ccc5-4f08-510e-8697-e8982768e8cb" "answer-ba2a5cbf-ee94-53c5-a9d9-e968b01ef75a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1906510-55d6-5ff1-aac1-ff539fe0295c" :answer/id #uuid "f1906510-55d6-5ff1-aac1-ff539fe0295c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4be9c323-4eec-53ad-ae4b-9e07303bdcb4" :answer/id #uuid "4be9c323-4eec-53ad-ae4b-9e07303bdcb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e1fc3e9-6b7e-5bb9-b995-f286738d3db4" :answer/id #uuid "9e1fc3e9-6b7e-5bb9-b995-f286738d3db4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43e0ccc5-4f08-510e-8697-e8982768e8cb" :answer/id #uuid "43e0ccc5-4f08-510e-8697-e8982768e8cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba2a5cbf-ee94-53c5-a9d9-e968b01ef75a" :answer/id #uuid "ba2a5cbf-ee94-53c5-a9d9-e968b01ef75a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb84f58e-e39d-5a83-ae84-6b21925b6b81" :question/id #uuid "bb84f58e-e39d-5a83-ae84-6b21925b6b81" :question/math-academy-id "q-68895" :question/problem "At Chan's SuperMarket, there are three different bottles of spicy peach BBQ sauce:\n\n- The $17$-ounce $A$-brand bottle costs $$14.96\\,.$\n\n- The $19$-ounce $B$-brand bottle costs $$15.96\\,.$\n\n- The $18$-ounce $C$-brand bottle costs $$15.66\\,.$\n\nWhich brand of spicy peach BBQ sauce is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three brands. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of ounces.  \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in the $A$-brand bottle,  we get\n\n$$\n14.96÷17=0.88\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of the $A$-brand bottle is $$0.88.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in the $B$-brand bottle,  we get\n\n$$\n15.96÷19=0.84\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of the $B$-brand bottle is $$0.84.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in the $C$-brand bottle,  we get\n\n$$\n15.66÷18=0.87\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of the $C$-brand bottle is $$0.87.$\n\nFrom the above, we see that brand $B$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, brand $B$ is the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc7e3b27-802f-5d1f-b82a-44ba7a6e2fd1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc7e3b27-802f-5d1f-b82a-44ba7a6e2fd1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc7e3b27-802f-5d1f-b82a-44ba7a6e2fd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d97ffa70-b7cb-5140-b264-2ad19f2c7d47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc3e8545-31b8-59e4-85d0-0edecdd41e74" "answer-d97ffa70-b7cb-5140-b264-2ad19f2c7d47" "answer-ef3fb457-320d-5b37-b82f-0ecf2efd41dd" "answer-6e71fa60-c756-5470-8cf7-803ae8c3745a" "answer-8a979450-a206-559b-9ca2-6f2697142e4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc3e8545-31b8-59e4-85d0-0edecdd41e74" :answer/id #uuid "fc3e8545-31b8-59e4-85d0-0edecdd41e74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Brand $A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d97ffa70-b7cb-5140-b264-2ad19f2c7d47" :answer/id #uuid "d97ffa70-b7cb-5140-b264-2ad19f2c7d47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Brand $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef3fb457-320d-5b37-b82f-0ecf2efd41dd" :answer/id #uuid "ef3fb457-320d-5b37-b82f-0ecf2efd41dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Brand $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e71fa60-c756-5470-8cf7-803ae8c3745a" :answer/id #uuid "6e71fa60-c756-5470-8cf7-803ae8c3745a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Brands$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a979450-a206-559b-9ca2-6f2697142e4e" :answer/id #uuid "8a979450-a206-559b-9ca2-6f2697142e4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Brands$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-689d0fea-adfc-579c-9b61-c303964b2aec" :question/id #uuid "689d0fea-adfc-579c-9b61-c303964b2aec" :question/math-academy-id "q-68942" :question/problem "Bart and two of his friends pooled money together to buy a bottle of blueberry juice whose unit price is $$12.50$ per gallon. How much juice should Bart get if he only puts in $1$ dollar?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$12.50$ per gallon (dollars per gallon). To find the amount of blueberry juice that Bart could get for $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in gallon per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n12.50\\,\\text{dollars per gallon}\\,\\to \\,1÷12.5=0.08\\,\\text{gallons per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.08$ gallons per dollar. Therefore, Bart should get only $0.08$ gallons of the blueberry juice." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d75103d-90d7-57fe-8873-8e0f248cd292"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d75103d-90d7-57fe-8873-8e0f248cd292" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d75103d-90d7-57fe-8873-8e0f248cd292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68f137ee-f9d5-51f6-863f-80c639fff59c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6d166949-53b6-57c4-b1ee-60eaf349f517" "answer-7d484d84-b818-5242-95b2-ad6851eff3a9" "answer-68f137ee-f9d5-51f6-863f-80c639fff59c" "answer-26149639-344a-5daf-ab19-c899fbfeba5b" "answer-ab75b57d-dd4a-541b-b489-edea4ed691a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d166949-53b6-57c4-b1ee-60eaf349f517" :answer/id #uuid "6d166949-53b6-57c4-b1ee-60eaf349f517" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.04$ gallons" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d484d84-b818-5242-95b2-ad6851eff3a9" :answer/id #uuid "7d484d84-b818-5242-95b2-ad6851eff3a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.06$ gallons" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68f137ee-f9d5-51f6-863f-80c639fff59c" :answer/id #uuid "68f137ee-f9d5-51f6-863f-80c639fff59c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.08$ gallons" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26149639-344a-5daf-ab19-c899fbfeba5b" :answer/id #uuid "26149639-344a-5daf-ab19-c899fbfeba5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.4$ gallons" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab75b57d-dd4a-541b-b489-edea4ed691a6" :answer/id #uuid "ab75b57d-dd4a-541b-b489-edea4ed691a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.8$ gallons" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-517daee3-2d5a-5b03-be17-46f0dc74f72d" :question/id #uuid "517daee3-2d5a-5b03-be17-46f0dc74f72d" :question/math-academy-id "q-68939" :question/problem "Sarah, a registered nurse, charges $$1.25$ per minute for her work in a rehabilitation center. How long should she work for $1$ dollar?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$1.25$ per minute (dollars per minute). To find how many minutes Sarah should work  for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in minutes per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n1.25\\,\\text{dollars per minute}\\,\\to \\,1÷1.25=0.8\\,\\text{minutes per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.8$ minutes per dollar. Therefore, Sarah should work  $0.8$ minutes for $1$ dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-758a60a4-f764-5094-8cfe-aecafffe9082"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-758a60a4-f764-5094-8cfe-aecafffe9082" :answer-field/id #uuid "758a60a4-f764-5094-8cfe-aecafffe9082" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-94b4c6af-75f2-5fd2-8c5f-0fe9eaace917" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ea42e11-a0cf-5e31-8b12-e03a025151ec" "answer-6d807fcc-ea83-559c-8a44-f0783cbcfabf" "answer-592de0bc-19b2-5beb-ad20-e19a8e44e2a3" "answer-94b4c6af-75f2-5fd2-8c5f-0fe9eaace917" "answer-83d04995-ab82-5357-8740-397f838e0200"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ea42e11-a0cf-5e31-8b12-e03a025151ec" :answer/id #uuid "6ea42e11-a0cf-5e31-8b12-e03a025151ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.4$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d807fcc-ea83-559c-8a44-f0783cbcfabf" :answer/id #uuid "6d807fcc-ea83-559c-8a44-f0783cbcfabf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.6$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-592de0bc-19b2-5beb-ad20-e19a8e44e2a3" :answer/id #uuid "592de0bc-19b2-5beb-ad20-e19a8e44e2a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.7$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94b4c6af-75f2-5fd2-8c5f-0fe9eaace917" :answer/id #uuid "94b4c6af-75f2-5fd2-8c5f-0fe9eaace917" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.8$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83d04995-ab82-5357-8740-397f838e0200" :answer/id #uuid "83d04995-ab82-5357-8740-397f838e0200" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.9$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1dc8a6fb-a221-5a8e-ae1b-b509f998884f" :question/id #uuid "1dc8a6fb-a221-5a8e-ae1b-b509f998884f" :question/math-academy-id "q-355713" :question/problem "At the supply store, the unit price of rope is $$10$ per meter. How many meters of rope can Maya buy for $$1?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$10$ per meter (dollars per meter). To find how many meters of rope she can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in meters per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n10\\,\\text{dollars per meter}\\,\\to \\,1÷10=0.1\\,\\text{meters per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.1$ meters per dollar. Therefore, Maya can buy $0.1$ meters of rope for $1$ dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6798386e-aa5b-5822-9c5c-5d9a8e3bdd36"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6798386e-aa5b-5822-9c5c-5d9a8e3bdd36" :answer-field/id #uuid "6798386e-aa5b-5822-9c5c-5d9a8e3bdd36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-17bc08cc-ce68-54a0-88b0-250d3b17d066" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54cab23f-4a0c-5a15-b2b6-fbddfa6cac4e" "answer-17bc08cc-ce68-54a0-88b0-250d3b17d066" "answer-8ad4b9e6-2690-5992-94d5-668e303ff84f" "answer-899dd541-8347-59be-b1a9-c8801116595a" "answer-57c4d878-c44e-5692-852e-cd7b918f8a09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54cab23f-4a0c-5a15-b2b6-fbddfa6cac4e" :answer/id #uuid "54cab23f-4a0c-5a15-b2b6-fbddfa6cac4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.01$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17bc08cc-ce68-54a0-88b0-250d3b17d066" :answer/id #uuid "17bc08cc-ce68-54a0-88b0-250d3b17d066" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.1$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ad4b9e6-2690-5992-94d5-668e303ff84f" :answer/id #uuid "8ad4b9e6-2690-5992-94d5-668e303ff84f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.2$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-899dd541-8347-59be-b1a9-c8801116595a" :answer/id #uuid "899dd541-8347-59be-b1a9-c8801116595a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.25$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57c4d878-c44e-5692-852e-cd7b918f8a09" :answer/id #uuid "57c4d878-c44e-5692-852e-cd7b918f8a09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.5$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e6dd181-7d62-533c-99d8-31ea5383ac30" :question/id #uuid "7e6dd181-7d62-533c-99d8-31ea5383ac30" :question/math-academy-id "q-68507" :question/problem "Mia charges $$0.20$ per minute for babysitting. For how long did she babysit if she earns $1$ dollar?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$0.2$ per minute (dollars per minute). To find how many minutes she babysits for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in minutes per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n0.2\\,\\text{dollars per minute}\\,\\to \\,1÷0.2=5\\,\\text{minutes per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $5$ minutes per dollar. Therefore, Mia babysits $5$ minutes for $1$ dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fd5b6bad-d609-5af7-a23d-e7ae41146ca0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fd5b6bad-d609-5af7-a23d-e7ae41146ca0" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5b6bad-d609-5af7-a23d-e7ae41146ca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e573580-6cee-55a0-a9d6-143660f23dc7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-abd8eae1-1830-5d87-9c09-fdcfe19969d1" "answer-d98608bc-b256-528b-afa5-92f92633b657" "answer-1a80ed70-1bfc-5c97-b651-ba289de9f0ee" "answer-6e573580-6cee-55a0-a9d6-143660f23dc7" "answer-ad24ea14-6842-5cc2-87ae-52d340f8a824"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abd8eae1-1830-5d87-9c09-fdcfe19969d1" :answer/id #uuid "abd8eae1-1830-5d87-9c09-fdcfe19969d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d98608bc-b256-528b-afa5-92f92633b657" :answer/id #uuid "d98608bc-b256-528b-afa5-92f92633b657" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a80ed70-1bfc-5c97-b651-ba289de9f0ee" :answer/id #uuid "1a80ed70-1bfc-5c97-b651-ba289de9f0ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e573580-6cee-55a0-a9d6-143660f23dc7" :answer/id #uuid "6e573580-6cee-55a0-a9d6-143660f23dc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad24ea14-6842-5cc2-87ae-52d340f8a824" :answer/id #uuid "ad24ea14-6842-5cc2-87ae-52d340f8a824" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8ca824bb-dbd7-559a-8d0c-91866baabae8" :question/id #uuid "8ca824bb-dbd7-559a-8d0c-91866baabae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-91919" :question/problem "At the vegetable market, the unit price for bananas is $$2.50$ per kilogram. How many kilograms of bananas can Mary buy with $$1?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$2.50$ per kilogram (dollars per kilogram). To find the number of kilograms of bananas that Mary can buy for $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in kilograms per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n2.50\\,\\text{dollars per kilogram}\\,\\to \\,1÷2.50=0.4\\,\\text{kilograms per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.4$ kilograms per dollar. Therefore, Mary can buy $0.4$ kilograms of bananas." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37a16aac-5fcd-5385-8c8e-82ce5e79b7c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37a16aac-5fcd-5385-8c8e-82ce5e79b7c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "37a16aac-5fcd-5385-8c8e-82ce5e79b7c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f450ccdf-fdf8-58ab-b3cb-f5dc2dd18c56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5acbe6d-8cf7-50d4-80c3-5d5ef31cbc64" "answer-142654a9-a855-540b-9fa9-55d2c199d63e" "answer-f450ccdf-fdf8-58ab-b3cb-f5dc2dd18c56" "answer-c793ad00-641c-5add-aae4-9d32c9831a88" "answer-209a2c44-f250-58f7-a31c-4136773ee413"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5acbe6d-8cf7-50d4-80c3-5d5ef31cbc64" :answer/id #uuid "a5acbe6d-8cf7-50d4-80c3-5d5ef31cbc64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.25$ kilograms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-142654a9-a855-540b-9fa9-55d2c199d63e" :answer/id #uuid "142654a9-a855-540b-9fa9-55d2c199d63e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.30$ kilograms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f450ccdf-fdf8-58ab-b3cb-f5dc2dd18c56" :answer/id #uuid "f450ccdf-fdf8-58ab-b3cb-f5dc2dd18c56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.4$ kilograms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c793ad00-641c-5add-aae4-9d32c9831a88" :answer/id #uuid "c793ad00-641c-5add-aae4-9d32c9831a88" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.45$ kilograms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-209a2c44-f250-58f7-a31c-4136773ee413" :answer/id #uuid "209a2c44-f250-58f7-a31c-4136773ee413" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.50$ kilograms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-55a58a08-8164-5352-9b75-43c62ba6ecc5" :tutorial/id #uuid "55a58a08-8164-5352-9b75-43c62ba6ecc5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 15086 :tutorial/title "Introduction" :tutorial/content "When we compare prices, it is often helpful to know the *unit price*. Knowing it helps us:\n\n- compare different products,\n\n- determine the total cost for a given amount,\n\n- decide which option is the better deal.\n\nFor example, suppose Lena wants to buy some apples. The price of apples at a nearby market is $\\[math]1.20/\\mathrm{lb}.$ How much would Lena pay for $4$ pounds of apples?\n\nThe unit price is $\\[/math]1.20$ per pound.  \n\nSince Lena is buying $4$ pounds, we multiply the unit price by the number of pounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1.20\\times 4 & =4.80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Lena would pay $\\[math]4.80$ for $4$ pounds of apples.\n\nWhenever we know the unit price and the quantity, we can find the total cost by multiplying:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total Cost} = \\text{Unit Price} \\times \\text{Quantity}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-be64d01c-4eb7-5332-b26c-97583b224a56" :tutorial/id #uuid "be64d01c-4eb7-5332-b26c-97583b224a56" :tutorial/math-academy-id 15097 :tutorial/title "Determining the Best Deal by Computing Unit Prices" :tutorial/content "Unit prices can be used to quantify how good of a deal a particular purchase is.\n\nFor example, suppose that a store sells two packs of shirts:\n\n- $3$ shirts for $\\[math]12$\n\n- $5$ shirts for $\\[/math]15$\n\nTo determine which pack is the better deal, we can compare their unit prices.\n\n- For the pack of $3$ shirts for $\\[math]12,$ dividing the total cost by the total number of shirts gives\n\n$$\n12 \\div 3 = 4.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price is $\\[/math]4.$\n\n- For the pack of $5$ shirts for $\\[math]15,$ dividing the total cost by the total number of shirts gives\n\n$$\n15 \\div 5 = 3.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price is $\\[/math]3.$\n\nNow we interpret the unit prices in the context of the problem.\n\n- In the pack of $3$ shirts for $\\[math]12,$ each shirt costs $\\[/math]4.$\n\n- In the pack of $5$ shirts for $\\[math]15,$ each shirt costs $\\[/math]3.$\n\nBased on the above, we conclude that the pack of $5$ shirts for $\\[math]15$ is the better deal because it has a lower unit price (meaning that each shirt costs less)." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-18f05709-44a6-59bc-962c-dbf491ad7501" :tutorial/id #uuid "18f05709-44a6-59bc-962c-dbf491ad7501" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3106 :tutorial/title "Reciprocal Unit Prices" :tutorial/content "For every unit price in \"dollars per item\", there is also a **reciprocal unit price** in \"items per dollar\".\n\nFor example, suppose that a store sells fabric for $\\[math]2$ per yard. Taking the reciprocal, we have\n\n$$\n2 \\,\\textrm{dollars per yard} \\quad\\rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}  \\,\\textrm{yards per dollar} .\n$$\n\nSo, if we have $\\[/math]1,$ then we can buy $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ of a yard of fabric." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "activity-24b39a23-bcdc-53b3-a773-ff2a2a0400ae" :activity/id #uuid "24b39a23-bcdc-53b3-a773-ff2a2a0400ae" :activity/title "Working With Unit Prices" :activity/type :activity.type/lesson :activity/scope "topic-04654553-f8da-5ec9-a27d-ee5bae447da5" :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :activity/steps ["step-7f189f23-779a-5ab6-9245-89a7a070f017" "step-b7fc4646-02d5-59f6-896d-aa9560955608" "step-235b590b-52bc-52e8-a4ef-db453fdea765" "step-1de7948d-68f8-5999-953c-8acb8be31016" "step-aebf2791-ae4f-5ea2-8312-994b316164b5" "step-30f25678-f130-575f-b357-4ffe8b59f407"] :activity/first-step "step-7f189f23-779a-5ab6-9245-89a7a070f017" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7f189f23-779a-5ab6-9245-89a7a070f017" :step/id #uuid "7f189f23-779a-5ab6-9245-89a7a070f017" :step/content "tutorial-55a58a08-8164-5352-9b75-43c62ba6ecc5" :step/math-academy-id 616950 :step/next "step-b7fc4646-02d5-59f6-896d-aa9560955608" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b7fc4646-02d5-59f6-896d-aa9560955608" :step/id #uuid "b7fc4646-02d5-59f6-896d-aa9560955608" :step/content "knowledge-point-d550bb4f-72a6-5b74-b050-8fdc2af6b23f" :step/math-academy-id 616951 :step/next "step-235b590b-52bc-52e8-a4ef-db453fdea765" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-235b590b-52bc-52e8-a4ef-db453fdea765" :step/id #uuid "235b590b-52bc-52e8-a4ef-db453fdea765" :step/content "tutorial-be64d01c-4eb7-5332-b26c-97583b224a56" :step/math-academy-id 616954 :step/next "step-1de7948d-68f8-5999-953c-8acb8be31016" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1de7948d-68f8-5999-953c-8acb8be31016" :step/id #uuid "1de7948d-68f8-5999-953c-8acb8be31016" :step/content "knowledge-point-04d9118c-9cc2-5bb5-a7c4-ce43be06a65d" :step/math-academy-id 616955 :step/next "step-aebf2791-ae4f-5ea2-8312-994b316164b5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-aebf2791-ae4f-5ea2-8312-994b316164b5" :step/id #uuid "aebf2791-ae4f-5ea2-8312-994b316164b5" :step/content "tutorial-18f05709-44a6-59bc-962c-dbf491ad7501" :step/math-academy-id 616958 :step/next "step-30f25678-f130-575f-b357-4ffe8b59f407" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-30f25678-f130-575f-b357-4ffe8b59f407" :step/id #uuid "30f25678-f130-575f-b357-4ffe8b59f407" :step/content "knowledge-point-1321abcb-7c99-5fef-b4fb-975ae5652b90" :step/math-academy-id 616959 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339020 :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=25$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+5 \\\\ y=-2t, \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (2t+5)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3}t)^{2} & =25 \\\\ (4{t}^{2}+20t+25)+4{t}^{2}+12{t}^{2} & =25 \\\\ 20{t}^{2}+20t+25 & =25 \\\\ 20{t}^{2}+20t & =0 \\\\ 20t(t+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+5=5 \\\\ y=-2(0)=0 \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(5,0,0).$\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2(-1)+5=3 \\\\ y=-2(-1)=2 \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}(-1)=-2\\sqrt{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(5,0,0)$ and $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3}).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403440 :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=t, \\\\ z=-t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2(1+t)^{2}+6(t)^{2}+(-t)^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2(1+2t+{t}^{2})+6{t}^{2}+{t}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2+4t+2{t}^{2}+6{t}^{2}+{t}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 9{t}^{2}+4t & =0 \\\\ t(9t+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-\\frac{4}{9}$ and $t=0.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\frac{4}{9}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1+(-\\frac{4}{9})=\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ y=-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ z=-(-\\frac{4}{9})=\\frac{4}{9},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9}).$\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1+0=1 \\\\ y=0 \\\\ z=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(1,0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9})$ and $(1,0,0).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186162647 :question/answer-fields 17592186161174] [:db/retract 17592186161264 :answer-field/choices 17592186161265] [:db/retract 17592186161264 :answer-field/choices 17592186161266] [:db/retract 17592186161264 :answer-field/choices 17592186161267] [:db/retract 17592186161264 :answer-field/choices 17592186161268] [:db/retract 17592186161264 :answer-field/choices 17592186161269] {:db/id 17592186162014 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f8b0f486-8442-538c-933a-d85ad556ff51"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162662 :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-10$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 15\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =-10.$ Computing $A-(-10)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+10I & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 15\\end{aligned}]+10[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 25 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-5{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{26}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}25 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161264 :answer-field/correct "answer-9d276ed0-9aab-5f35-92de-cd40b3be996e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f44ec68-5673-5d17-a202-807989a0d5ce" "answer-9d276ed0-9aab-5f35-92de-cd40b3be996e" "answer-07faab27-15f7-5312-8b38-59ad02f72521" "answer-8b205150-ffac-59f3-b8f8-30947cc22faa" "answer-6c89eafa-421f-5962-9af4-946ba03a1964"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f44ec68-5673-5d17-a202-807989a0d5ce" :answer/id #uuid "2f44ec68-5673-5d17-a202-807989a0d5ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d276ed0-9aab-5f35-92de-cd40b3be996e" :answer/id #uuid "9d276ed0-9aab-5f35-92de-cd40b3be996e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}25 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07faab27-15f7-5312-8b38-59ad02f72521" :answer/id #uuid "07faab27-15f7-5312-8b38-59ad02f72521" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b205150-ffac-59f3-b8f8-30947cc22faa" :answer/id #uuid "8b205150-ffac-59f3-b8f8-30947cc22faa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}25 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c89eafa-421f-5962-9af4-946ba03a1964" :answer/id #uuid "6c89eafa-421f-5962-9af4-946ba03a1964" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}[\\begin{aligned}25 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8b0f486-8442-538c-933a-d85ad556ff51" :question/id #uuid "f8b0f486-8442-538c-933a-d85ad556ff51" :question/math-academy-id "q-95716" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 17\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =1.$ Computing $A-1I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-I & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 17\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{4}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=5.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7f1f6569-2671-58ca-aa36-0fefdf95c894"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7f1f6569-2671-58ca-aa36-0fefdf95c894" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1f6569-2671-58ca-aa36-0fefdf95c894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fec25ec0-ae75-52d4-992b-cbf821a92df5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-891a910a-dee7-5f7a-b066-db75538859fa" "answer-fec25ec0-ae75-52d4-992b-cbf821a92df5" "answer-1a866929-0beb-5a32-8959-34966c6e6ad9" "answer-7d73673d-5635-5b93-8b05-960db3e3f68f" "answer-28cc6daa-99e2-5439-a52d-8c74f6f8d55b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-891a910a-dee7-5f7a-b066-db75538859fa" :answer/id #uuid "891a910a-dee7-5f7a-b066-db75538859fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fec25ec0-ae75-52d4-992b-cbf821a92df5" :answer/id #uuid "fec25ec0-ae75-52d4-992b-cbf821a92df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a866929-0beb-5a32-8959-34966c6e6ad9" :answer/id #uuid "1a866929-0beb-5a32-8959-34966c6e6ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d73673d-5635-5b93-8b05-960db3e3f68f" :answer/id #uuid "7d73673d-5635-5b93-8b05-960db3e3f68f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28cc6daa-99e2-5439-a52d-8c74f6f8d55b" :answer/id #uuid "28cc6daa-99e2-5439-a52d-8c74f6f8d55b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f7834130-0260-5c43-bf45-c2988a6f854e" :activity/id #uuid "f7834130-0260-5c43-bf45-c2988a6f854e" :activity/title "The Spectral Theorem" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049849 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-d7e437ea-03ba-522c-8c2f-e2da5dacae70" "step-cd9e99be-c8ca-50d9-aacd-09344ae9dae2" "step-67e20c48-efe2-5fd4-8d06-cb1125f84345" "step-b38fd098-3465-5c13-8a12-93f1b35b5090" "step-dc9cbb5e-30fb-5f9a-8c8a-71b1f6f7926c"] :activity/first-step "step-d7e437ea-03ba-522c-8c2f-e2da5dacae70" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d7e437ea-03ba-522c-8c2f-e2da5dacae70" :step/id #uuid "d7e437ea-03ba-522c-8c2f-e2da5dacae70" :step/content 17592186162647 :step/next "step-cd9e99be-c8ca-50d9-aacd-09344ae9dae2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cd9e99be-c8ca-50d9-aacd-09344ae9dae2" :step/id #uuid "cd9e99be-c8ca-50d9-aacd-09344ae9dae2" :step/content 17592186162662 :step/next "step-67e20c48-efe2-5fd4-8d06-cb1125f84345" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-67e20c48-efe2-5fd4-8d06-cb1125f84345" :step/id #uuid "67e20c48-efe2-5fd4-8d06-cb1125f84345" :step/content "question-f8b0f486-8442-538c-933a-d85ad556ff51" :step/next "step-b38fd098-3465-5c13-8a12-93f1b35b5090" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b38fd098-3465-5c13-8a12-93f1b35b5090" :step/id #uuid "b38fd098-3465-5c13-8a12-93f1b35b5090" :step/content 17592186378065 :step/next "step-dc9cbb5e-30fb-5f9a-8c8a-71b1f6f7926c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dc9cbb5e-30fb-5f9a-8c8a-71b1f6f7926c" :step/id #uuid "dc9cbb5e-30fb-5f9a-8c8a-71b1f6f7926c" :step/content 17592186395066 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152222 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4868b354-15b9-5c4c-bfd0-122202f40c50"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186360586 :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{4}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{4}(R))={4}^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-872bbc86-b2d9-5fc0-a340-666aa227cedf" "question-300def0f-69c7-5821-80a9-ead2c4071d95"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-872bbc86-b2d9-5fc0-a340-666aa227cedf" :question/id #uuid "872bbc86-b2d9-5fc0-a340-666aa227cedf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95225" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $12?$\n\nI. ${R}^{12}$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 4}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 4$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}_{11}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $11$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{12})=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3\\times 4}(R))=3\\cdot 4=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{11}[t])=11+1=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b5c8af9-d959-569a-8058-100af23b2c12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b5c8af9-d959-569a-8058-100af23b2c12" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b5c8af9-d959-569a-8058-100af23b2c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b2867c1c-1f11-5f60-8eeb-04a47f542fab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6d9093c-41de-586e-8b9a-a4e06e3dceda" "answer-c9096bb1-9011-5dc6-aea5-546459a5a73c" "answer-2d9255a3-f808-53ab-9a1d-bce0b2aee8d7" "answer-b2867c1c-1f11-5f60-8eeb-04a47f542fab" "answer-4ad4f74f-98bf-5d22-9457-443e51eb0e44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6d9093c-41de-586e-8b9a-a4e06e3dceda" :answer/id #uuid "a6d9093c-41de-586e-8b9a-a4e06e3dceda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9096bb1-9011-5dc6-aea5-546459a5a73c" :answer/id #uuid "c9096bb1-9011-5dc6-aea5-546459a5a73c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d9255a3-f808-53ab-9a1d-bce0b2aee8d7" :answer/id #uuid "2d9255a3-f808-53ab-9a1d-bce0b2aee8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2867c1c-1f11-5f60-8eeb-04a47f542fab" :answer/id #uuid "b2867c1c-1f11-5f60-8eeb-04a47f542fab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ad4f74f-98bf-5d22-9457-443e51eb0e44" :answer/id #uuid "4ad4f74f-98bf-5d22-9457-443e51eb0e44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-300def0f-69c7-5821-80a9-ead2c4071d95" :question/id #uuid "300def0f-69c7-5821-80a9-ead2c4071d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-95228" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $18?$\n\nI. ${R}_{17}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $17$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 3}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}^{17}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{17}[t])=17+1=18.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6\\times 3}(R))=6\\cdot 3=18.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{17})=17\\ne 18.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ae053587-50f1-5f8c-b674-29dc44c5f648"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ae053587-50f1-5f8c-b674-29dc44c5f648" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae053587-50f1-5f8c-b674-29dc44c5f648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-32aca3cf-a5e2-53e0-9465-8c5812ddcb24" :answer-field/choices ["answer-32aca3cf-a5e2-53e0-9465-8c5812ddcb24" "answer-9317dd78-6bb1-51d8-9527-c7283331155e" "answer-ce013736-d830-5648-bf13-13959d355826" "answer-500ce576-4c92-5f17-8883-d14fb5dd6073" "answer-cab46aea-83c2-537f-b7c2-3ead6ff50e30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32aca3cf-a5e2-53e0-9465-8c5812ddcb24" :answer/id #uuid "32aca3cf-a5e2-53e0-9465-8c5812ddcb24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9317dd78-6bb1-51d8-9527-c7283331155e" :answer/id #uuid "9317dd78-6bb1-51d8-9527-c7283331155e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce013736-d830-5648-bf13-13959d355826" :answer/id #uuid "ce013736-d830-5648-bf13-13959d355826" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-500ce576-4c92-5f17-8883-d14fb5dd6073" :answer/id #uuid "500ce576-4c92-5f17-8883-d14fb5dd6073" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cab46aea-83c2-537f-b7c2-3ead6ff50e30" :answer/id #uuid "cab46aea-83c2-537f-b7c2-3ead6ff50e30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152221 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f0776bb6-a5c9-57f2-a5dc-9cd00549186b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f0776bb6-a5c9-57f2-a5dc-9cd00549186b" :question/id #uuid "f0776bb6-a5c9-57f2-a5dc-9cd00549186b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95233" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\nI. ${R}^{750}$\n\nII. ${R}^{\\infty },$ the vector space of infinite real sequences\n\nIII. ${\\text{M}}_{50}(R),$ the vector space of all $50\\times 50$ matrices over $R$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- ${R}^{\\infty }$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of sequences is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n\\{{e}_{1},\\,{e}_{2},\\,…,{e}_{n}\\},\\,n\\in N\n$$\n\nwhere, for each $j\\in \\{1,2,…,n\\},$\n\n$$\n{e}_{j}=(0,…,0,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{1,}_{{↑}_{{j}^{\\text{th}}\\text{ position}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0,…).\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{x}_{i}{e}_{i}=0\n$$\n\nif and only if ${x}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of ${R}^{\\infty }$ of size $n,$ which imples that  ${R}^{\\infty }$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${R}^{750}$ and ${\\text{M}}_{50}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{750})=750,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{50}(R))={50}^{2}=2\\,500\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-01e9553e-a36d-5ce4-9531-7c5e67d94d60"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-01e9553e-a36d-5ce4-9531-7c5e67d94d60" :answer-field/id #uuid "01e9553e-a36d-5ce4-9531-7c5e67d94d60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-08461b80-8ee5-589b-a179-259194936ce8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-771ae68d-4a83-5f4f-9dcc-443975716b04" "answer-08461b80-8ee5-589b-a179-259194936ce8" "answer-c31ee08d-68d0-5e26-b97b-8161c20fe5c3" "answer-b2a39110-5421-5df4-bfb4-13a5169af020" "answer-5af31435-c11c-5c3f-b06e-2a10c6c1c500"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-771ae68d-4a83-5f4f-9dcc-443975716b04" :answer/id #uuid "771ae68d-4a83-5f4f-9dcc-443975716b04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08461b80-8ee5-589b-a179-259194936ce8" :answer/id #uuid "08461b80-8ee5-589b-a179-259194936ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c31ee08d-68d0-5e26-b97b-8161c20fe5c3" :answer/id #uuid "c31ee08d-68d0-5e26-b97b-8161c20fe5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2a39110-5421-5df4-bfb4-13a5169af020" :answer/id #uuid "b2a39110-5421-5df4-bfb4-13a5169af020" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5af31435-c11c-5c3f-b06e-2a10c6c1c500" :answer/id #uuid "5af31435-c11c-5c3f-b06e-2a10c6c1c500" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4868b354-15b9-5c4c-bfd0-122202f40c50" :question/id #uuid "4868b354-15b9-5c4c-bfd0-122202f40c50" :question/math-academy-id "q-106882" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 5}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 5$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 2}(R)$ contains $3\\cdot 2=6$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 5}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6\\times 5}(R))=6\\cdot 5=30.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b725a1ed-492c-532e-82ae-acdc74378877"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b725a1ed-492c-532e-82ae-acdc74378877" :answer-field/id #uuid "b725a1ed-492c-532e-82ae-acdc74378877" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-98625c99-1d21-5d81-8b45-7668916611fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c68081df-1e95-51e2-8875-d1f0093b0cbe" "answer-ca864cf8-1d57-54a6-bac6-6cdaa11ca7a5" "answer-2bd1a089-11bd-5537-b24d-b5320d066943" "answer-7b41ed65-ebd8-5e8a-9322-4359d606455b" "answer-98625c99-1d21-5d81-8b45-7668916611fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c68081df-1e95-51e2-8875-d1f0093b0cbe" :answer/id #uuid "c68081df-1e95-51e2-8875-d1f0093b0cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca864cf8-1d57-54a6-bac6-6cdaa11ca7a5" :answer/id #uuid "ca864cf8-1d57-54a6-bac6-6cdaa11ca7a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bd1a089-11bd-5537-b24d-b5320d066943" :answer/id #uuid "2bd1a089-11bd-5537-b24d-b5320d066943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b41ed65-ebd8-5e8a-9322-4359d606455b" :answer/id #uuid "7b41ed65-ebd8-5e8a-9322-4359d606455b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98625c99-1d21-5d81-8b45-7668916611fe" :answer/id #uuid "98625c99-1d21-5d81-8b45-7668916611fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8fd7c257-aa59-5f20-b67e-9f32e957099a" :activity/id #uuid "8fd7c257-aa59-5f20-b67e-9f32e957099a" :activity/title "Dimension in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049808 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-a70eb95a-1d4a-5112-b093-41836097c112" "step-6ac3edfc-26f8-589b-8f2c-b805c5ecd692" "step-9ee124b4-4e89-5c70-ae8c-f8a1677ea468" "step-7b787e2b-3bc8-5c8f-b9c3-b74f50bd3683" "step-8c095d32-ef2b-570d-930d-b9c7020f763d"] :activity/first-step "step-a70eb95a-1d4a-5112-b093-41836097c112" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a70eb95a-1d4a-5112-b093-41836097c112" :step/id #uuid "a70eb95a-1d4a-5112-b093-41836097c112" :step/content 17592186360586 :step/next "step-6ac3edfc-26f8-589b-8f2c-b805c5ecd692" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6ac3edfc-26f8-589b-8f2c-b805c5ecd692" :step/id #uuid "6ac3edfc-26f8-589b-8f2c-b805c5ecd692" :step/content "question-872bbc86-b2d9-5fc0-a340-666aa227cedf" :step/next "step-9ee124b4-4e89-5c70-ae8c-f8a1677ea468" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9ee124b4-4e89-5c70-ae8c-f8a1677ea468" :step/id #uuid "9ee124b4-4e89-5c70-ae8c-f8a1677ea468" :step/content "question-300def0f-69c7-5821-80a9-ead2c4071d95" :step/next "step-7b787e2b-3bc8-5c8f-b9c3-b74f50bd3683" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7b787e2b-3bc8-5c8f-b9c3-b74f50bd3683" :step/id #uuid "7b787e2b-3bc8-5c8f-b9c3-b74f50bd3683" :step/content "question-f0776bb6-a5c9-57f2-a5dc-9cd00549186b" :step/next "step-8c095d32-ef2b-570d-930d-b9c7020f763d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8c095d32-ef2b-570d-930d-b9c7020f763d" :step/id #uuid "8c095d32-ef2b-570d-930d-b9c7020f763d" :step/content "question-4868b354-15b9-5c4c-bfd0-122202f40c50" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115356 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-743cb560-d24b-5701-9107-2d76831f26b0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-743cb560-d24b-5701-9107-2d76831f26b0" :question/id #uuid "743cb560-d24b-5701-9107-2d76831f26b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162648" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+(1+t)\\,j+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $1+t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\nt-\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e73b358-a22b-50ef-9592-ee78086917fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e73b358-a22b-50ef-9592-ee78086917fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e73b358-a22b-50ef-9592-ee78086917fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cdf2e835-db95-5864-affb-01ff7cb2c729" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6b7976b-3f51-5c07-8e0f-1d2e78e5cbc1" "answer-68c0ec99-c2fb-58f7-b7f5-fb61baf0c84f" "answer-8da11eb5-91be-5bf3-9fcf-acbbb9eaa5a1" "answer-7d3756b0-b0a2-556a-be88-863ea77b203d" "answer-cdf2e835-db95-5864-affb-01ff7cb2c729"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6b7976b-3f51-5c07-8e0f-1d2e78e5cbc1" :answer/id #uuid "c6b7976b-3f51-5c07-8e0f-1d2e78e5cbc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68c0ec99-c2fb-58f7-b7f5-fb61baf0c84f" :answer/id #uuid "68c0ec99-c2fb-58f7-b7f5-fb61baf0c84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8da11eb5-91be-5bf3-9fcf-acbbb9eaa5a1" :answer/id #uuid "8da11eb5-91be-5bf3-9fcf-acbbb9eaa5a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d3756b0-b0a2-556a-be88-863ea77b203d" :answer/id #uuid "7d3756b0-b0a2-556a-be88-863ea77b203d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdf2e835-db95-5864-affb-01ff7cb2c729" :answer/id #uuid "cdf2e835-db95-5864-affb-01ff7cb2c729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dd432b0a-1c26-5d37-8911-e5b811490135"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dd432b0a-1c26-5d37-8911-e5b811490135" :question/id #uuid "dd432b0a-1c26-5d37-8911-e5b811490135" :question/math-academy-id "q-127462" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{1}=\\frac{y-(-5)}{0}=\\frac{z-1}{9}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{y+5}{0}=\\frac{z-1}{9},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y+5}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=-5:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1+9t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y+5}{0}$ part and instead write $y=-5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{9},\\,y=-5\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4525723d-b5cd-5648-a3e1-1f8bec32accd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4525723d-b5cd-5648-a3e1-1f8bec32accd" :answer-field/id #uuid "4525723d-b5cd-5648-a3e1-1f8bec32accd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-553addc8-18e6-53d9-9334-7c785c7ad81b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a750839-2164-533a-a44a-d12f1239ee58" "answer-21da8be1-01fa-5395-a6d1-693fba89579e" "answer-a18e13dc-ae24-5ed7-8084-0bc94766af44" "answer-553addc8-18e6-53d9-9334-7c785c7ad81b" "answer-85c6789f-ffce-5244-91d7-4630e5c1a765"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a750839-2164-533a-a44a-d12f1239ee58" :answer/id #uuid "6a750839-2164-533a-a44a-d12f1239ee58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{1}=\\frac{z+1}{9},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21da8be1-01fa-5395-a6d1-693fba89579e" :answer/id #uuid "21da8be1-01fa-5395-a6d1-693fba89579e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{z+1}{9},\\,y=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a18e13dc-ae24-5ed7-8084-0bc94766af44" :answer/id #uuid "a18e13dc-ae24-5ed7-8084-0bc94766af44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{z+1}{9},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-553addc8-18e6-53d9-9334-7c785c7ad81b" :answer/id #uuid "553addc8-18e6-53d9-9334-7c785c7ad81b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{9},\\,y=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85c6789f-ffce-5244-91d7-4630e5c1a765" :answer/id #uuid "85c6789f-ffce-5244-91d7-4630e5c1a765" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{z-1}{-9},\\,y=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064307 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02602311-35ef-53b7-9d8d-d64db15f3075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-02602311-35ef-53b7-9d8d-d64db15f3075" :question/id #uuid "02602311-35ef-53b7-9d8d-d64db15f3075" :question/math-academy-id "q-341724" :question/problem "Given that $y={(\\frac{1}{2x})}^{x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{(2x)}^{-x}\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny={(\\frac{1}{2x})}^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({(\\frac{1}{2x})}^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2x})) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2x}))+(x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2x}))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2x})+x\\cdot ((2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{(2x)^{2}})) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2x})-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y={(\\frac{1}{2x})}^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-{(\\frac{1}{2x})}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1) \\\\  & =-{(2x)}^{-x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a47a029c-812d-5ac8-b753-06da557530dc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a47a029c-812d-5ac8-b753-06da557530dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a47a029c-812d-5ac8-b753-06da557530dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f14cc015-61de-559e-9d6e-4f7e934ed9c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f14cc015-61de-559e-9d6e-4f7e934ed9c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f14cc015-61de-559e-9d6e-4f7e934ed9c4" :answer/id #uuid "f14cc015-61de-559e-9d6e-4f7e934ed9c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(2x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dbb0dde9-c40d-5e25-859f-e2de0b0b8937"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dbb0dde9-c40d-5e25-859f-e2de0b0b8937" :question/id #uuid "dbb0dde9-c40d-5e25-859f-e2de0b0b8937" :question/math-academy-id "q-75605" :question/problem "An eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]$ \ncorresponding to an eigenvalue $\\lambda =3k-2$ is $[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5k\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5k\\end{aligned}] & =(3k-2)[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5k\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -30+35k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6(3k-2) \\\\ (5k)(3k-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -30+35k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-18k+12 \\\\ 15{k}^{2}-10k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6=-18k+12 \\\\ -30+35k=15{k}^{2}-10k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-6=-18k+12\\,⟹\\,k=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=1$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-30+35k & =15{k}^{2}-10k \\\\ -30+35\\cdot 1 & =15\\cdot {1}^{2}-10\\cdot 1 \\\\ 5 & =5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76b6e9d4-78c1-58c7-893c-a4f2cb9f0a8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76b6e9d4-78c1-58c7-893c-a4f2cb9f0a8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "76b6e9d4-78c1-58c7-893c-a4f2cb9f0a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a457dd93-1e88-5e06-a387-62d51340e2b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77a2513c-453d-5a29-8fe9-2a67c6dc9c03" "answer-bee15731-1afa-57b9-a681-55ceed3bd405" "answer-a457dd93-1e88-5e06-a387-62d51340e2b2" "answer-9fbd3cfe-59fd-5bb3-8ca5-8b31a8b5e03c" "answer-8a34feff-d7af-5be0-bb1e-052359fe25b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77a2513c-453d-5a29-8fe9-2a67c6dc9c03" :answer/id #uuid "77a2513c-453d-5a29-8fe9-2a67c6dc9c03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bee15731-1afa-57b9-a681-55ceed3bd405" :answer/id #uuid "bee15731-1afa-57b9-a681-55ceed3bd405" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a457dd93-1e88-5e06-a387-62d51340e2b2" :answer/id #uuid "a457dd93-1e88-5e06-a387-62d51340e2b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fbd3cfe-59fd-5bb3-8ca5-8b31a8b5e03c" :answer/id #uuid "9fbd3cfe-59fd-5bb3-8ca5-8b31a8b5e03c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a34feff-d7af-5be0-bb1e-052359fe25b4" :answer/id #uuid "8a34feff-d7af-5be0-bb1e-052359fe25b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147615 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8bd4a768-e4d0-520a-9786-1699a6b9a16d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8bd4a768-e4d0-520a-9786-1699a6b9a16d" :question/id #uuid "8bd4a768-e4d0-520a-9786-1699a6b9a16d" :question/math-academy-id "q-117652" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b420afa755a7cd99e427fc7c1aa06ea745f0a177fa83c60dff5a1bcd354c7b79.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The solid is a **rectangular pyramid** since it has a rectangular base and the other $4$ triangular faces meet at a single point.   \n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a cube since not all of its faces are squares.\n\n- The solid is not a triangular prism because it does not have two triangular bases connected by parallel line segments.\n\n- The solid is not a triangular pyramid since its base is not triangular.\n\n- The solid is not a heptagonal pyramid since its base is not a heptagon." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48c22ba1-69cb-5865-8357-8ff9ef9b3c3a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48c22ba1-69cb-5865-8357-8ff9ef9b3c3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "48c22ba1-69cb-5865-8357-8ff9ef9b3c3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15f20bf7-c743-53d2-a83f-5accca0ed01f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05f7eac3-f058-5133-9c8a-7faa8e159655" "answer-563bf08c-2a81-52d3-8917-c5e7faf405b6" "answer-15f20bf7-c743-53d2-a83f-5accca0ed01f" "answer-aeb1606b-2d4f-5bc5-b01d-187b5a6cb832" "answer-d70aba4d-dd6d-5861-888e-94192eb1fd09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05f7eac3-f058-5133-9c8a-7faa8e159655" :answer/id #uuid "05f7eac3-f058-5133-9c8a-7faa8e159655" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Cube" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-563bf08c-2a81-52d3-8917-c5e7faf405b6" :answer/id #uuid "563bf08c-2a81-52d3-8917-c5e7faf405b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Heptagonal pyramid" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15f20bf7-c743-53d2-a83f-5accca0ed01f" :answer/id #uuid "15f20bf7-c743-53d2-a83f-5accca0ed01f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Rectangular pyramid" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aeb1606b-2d4f-5bc5-b01d-187b5a6cb832" :answer/id #uuid "aeb1606b-2d4f-5bc5-b01d-187b5a6cb832" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Triangular prism" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d70aba4d-dd6d-5861-888e-94192eb1fd09" :answer/id #uuid "d70aba4d-dd6d-5861-888e-94192eb1fd09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Triangular pyramid" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-13caabb2-fccc-503a-88a9-84f1640d4d82" :activity/id #uuid "13caabb2-fccc-503a-88a9-84f1640d4d82" :activity/title "Quiz 2" :